* C:\Users\Umart\OneDrive\Documents\GitHub\DIY-Record-Player\Simulation\riaa_preamp.asc
* Generated by LTspice 26.1.1 for Windows.
Vcart cart_emf 0 AC 1 0
Rcoil cart_mid cart_emf 485
Lcoil vin cart_mid 550m
Rin_load vin 0 47k
Cload vin 0 150p
X§X1 vin fb VCC VEE vout_raw OPA164x ;§pnba In+)In-)V+)V-)OUT
R2 nB fb 43.2k
C2 nB fb 1.8n
R1 vout_raw nB 511k
C1 vout_raw nB 6.2n
R0 fb nA 1k
C0 nA 0 8.2µ
C3 vout_ac_couple vout_raw 100n
Vcc VCC 0 12
Vee VEE 0 -12
.include OPA164x/OPA164x.lib
.ac dec 100 10 100k
* .op
.subckt IDEAL_OPAMP inP inN vp vn out
Ein out 0 inP inN 1MEG
Rin_ideal inP inN 1G
.ends IDEAL_OPAMP
* RIAA Phono Preamplifier - single channel (schematic version of riaa_preamp.cir)\nTopology: Douglas Self, "Small Signal Audio Design" - single active-stage, non-inverting feedback RIAA equalizer.\nOp-amp: OPA1642 via TI generic OPA164x macromodel (OPA164x/OPA164x.lib, pin order IN+ IN- VCC VEE OUT).\nX1 is drawn flipped vertically (M180) so IN+ is on top: VEE pin at top, VCC pin at bottom.\nLocal "0" = this channel's audio ground; ties to PSU VGND when integrated (see power_supply).
* Cartridge: AT-VM95E (4mV @ 1kHz, 485R, 550mH)\nCload = placeholder total shunt C (target 100-200pF)
* R0/C0: unity DC gain + ~20Hz subsonic pole (~7960us)
* R1*C1 = 3180us (50Hz)\nR2*C2 = 75us (2122Hz)
* Fallback for pure-topology checks: change X1's Value from OPA164x to IDEAL_OPAMP (supply pins unused by that model).
.backanno
.end
